Z||000000||FieroSoul||09-18-2001||08:12 PM||||  Okay, I have searched about 10 different ways but can't find anything on this...<BR>  What do I need to do to switch my tach/volt guage to the tach/oil pressure guage?  ||||reg||6
Z||000001||FieroSoul||09-19-2001||06:31 AM||||****Bump****||||reg||6
Z||000002||Carrolles||09-19-2001||07:32 AM||||I guess you must have an 84.  I seem to remember someone saying that they have a volt meter under the tach.<P>My 85SE has an oil pressure gauge under the tach.<P>I assume the tach/oil pressure gauge module would bolt up in place of yours.  You'd have to follow the trace on the circuit board to match the correct wires to make the pressure gauge work.  I'm not sure if the 84 has the proper oil pressure sender to drive the gauge.<P>Maybe someone else can help here.<P>Good luck,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroSoul||09-19-2001||01:22 PM||||  You are right on the money with all of assumptions. I am sure someone else has done this before. I think most people find an oil guage more useful than a voltmeter. Thanks for the reply.||||reg||6
Z||000004||FieroSoul||09-19-2001||06:57 PM||||**Bump**||||reg||6
Z||000005||Loki||09-19-2001||07:06 PM||||Just get new gauges from an 86 up and swap em out... Need the houseing for the aux gauges (above radio) everything is plug-n-play||||reg||1
Z||000006||FieroJoe||09-19-2001||10:44 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Loki:<BR><B>Just get new gauges from an 86 up and swap em out... Need the houseing for the aux gauges (above radio) everything is plug-n-play</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Not necessarily.  If you want to still have the coupe gauges, you'll need to determine whether the oil pressure sender that is used for the idiot light in the 84's also has another terminal for the oil pressure gauge.  Otherwise, if you just put the gauge in, it will still read as a voltmeter.<P>Also, about adding aux gauges.  Since that gauge package was not available until 86, they arent plug and play with a 84 or 85.  In those cars there will be NO wiring harness connector for the aux gauges.  No matter what model you have after 86 it will be there (I have aux gauges in my 87 coupe 4cyl).<P>Also, if you wish to add the 120 gauges to a 4 banger car you will need to switch out the circuit boards on the back of the tachs, just unbolt and swap, nothing challenging there.||||reg||1
Z||000007||FieroSoul||09-20-2001||05:53 AM||||  Thanks guys, I can't wait for my guage set to get here.||||reg||6
